# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
#  demo_app — Fastfile (Production-grade CICD)
#
#  iOS:     bundle exec fastlane ios <lane>
#  Android: bundle exec fastlane android <lane>
#
#  Lanes:
#    iOS:     sync_certs | beta | production | adhoc | build_only
#             refresh_profile | register_new_device | bump_version
#    Android: beta | production | build_only | bump_version
# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Shared helper — App Store Connect API Key
#
#  WHY API Key instead of App-Specific Password:
#  - App-Specific Password requires interactive 2FA → CI hangs waiting for OTP
#  - API Key is a service account, not blocked by 2FA 
#  - Can be revoked independently without affecting the main Apple ID
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
def asc_api_key
  app_store_connect_api_key(
    key_id:      ENV.fetch("ASC_KEY_ID",      ""),
    issuer_id:   ENV.fetch("ASC_ISSUER_ID",   ""),
    key_content: ENV.fetch("ASC_KEY_CONTENT", ""),
    # WHY duration 1200s: iOS builds typically take 15-25 min.
    # Default 500s may expire mid-build → signing fails.
    duration:    1200,
  )
end

# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Shared helper — Git release notes
#
#  WHY: Automatically pulls commit messages from git as changelog.
#  Lets QA know what changed in the build without asking the dev.
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
def release_notes
  changelog = `git log -10 --pretty=format:"• %s" --no-merges`.strip
  changelog.empty? ? "No changelog available" : changelog
end

# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Shared helper — Slack notify (only runs when webhook is set)
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
def notify_slack(message:, success: true, payload: {})
  # Slack removed — no webhook configured
end

# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
#  iOS Platform
# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
platform :ios do

  # WHY before_all runs before EVERY lane in this block:
  # setup_ci creates a temporary keychain on the CI runner (macOS GitHub-hosted)
  # and keeps it unlocked throughout the build.
  #
  # Without this → codesign will HANG indefinitely on CI waiting for a password
  # prompt that no one is there to enter → CI timeout after 40-60 min.
  #
  # On local machines, setup_ci is a complete no-op — fully safe.
  before_all do
    setup_ci
  end

  # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  #  sync_certs
  #  Run once when: setting up a new machine, cert expires (1 year), adding a bundle ID
  #  Do NOT run automatically on CI.
  #
  #  WHY readonly: false here but true on CI:
  #  - readonly: false = match is allowed to CREATE new certs/profiles if missing
  #  - readonly: true  = match only FETCHES existing certs, errors if not found
  #  CI always uses readonly: true to avoid accidentally creating duplicate certs
  # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  desc "Sync all certs + profiles from the match repo. Run once when setting up a new machine or when a cert expires."
  lane :sync_certs do
    api_key = asc_api_key
    ["development", "adhoc", "appstore"].each do |type|
      match(
        type:                    type,
        readonly:                false,
        api_key:                 api_key,
        app_identifier:          ENV["APP_IDENTIFIER"],
        git_url:                 ENV["MATCH_GIT_URL"],
        # WHY git_basic_authorization instead of SSH:
        # CI runners (GitHub Actions, AppCenter) don't have SSH keys set up.
        # HTTPS + token works across all environments.
        # Base64-encoding "x-access-token:<token>" is the format GitHub requires.
        git_basic_authorization: Base64.strict_encode64("x-access-token:#{ENV['MATCH_GIT_TOKEN']}"),
      )
    end
    UI.success "✅ All certs synced! Ready to build locally or on CI."
  end

  # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  #  beta
  #  Build .ipa → upload to TestFlight (internal testing)
  #
  #  Flow:
  #  1. Query ASC → get latest build number → +1
  #  2. match fetch cert + appstore profile
  #  3. gym build .ipa with manual signing
  #  4. pilot upload to TestFlight
  #  5. Slack notify
  # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  desc "Build .ipa and upload to TestFlight (internal testing)"
  lane :beta do
    api_key = asc_api_key

    # WHY query build number from ASC:
    # CI runners are ephemeral — the xcodeproj in the repo ALWAYS holds a stale build number.
    # Without incrementing correctly → Apple rejects "build number already exists".
    # latest_testflight_build_number queries the App Store Connect API in real-time.
    # initial_build_number: 0 → first ever build (no builds yet) returns 0, +1 = 1.
    latest_build = latest_testflight_build_number(
      api_key:              api_key,
      app_identifier:       ENV["APP_IDENTIFIER"],
      initial_build_number: 0,
    )
    new_build_number = latest_build + 1

    increment_build_number(
      build_number: new_build_number,
      xcodeproj:    "ios/demo_app.xcodeproj",
    )

    # WHY readonly: true on CI:
    # CI must not create new certs. Only fetch existing ones from the match repo.
    # If a cert is missing → fail explicitly rather than creating an unexpected cert.
    match(
      type:                    "appstore",
      readonly:                true,
      api_key:                 api_key,
      app_identifier:          ENV["APP_IDENTIFIER"],
      git_url:                 ENV["MATCH_GIT_URL"],
      git_basic_authorization: Base64.strict_encode64("x-access-token:#{ENV['MATCH_GIT_TOKEN']}"),
    )

    # WHY override CODE_SIGN_STYLE to Manual via xcargs:
    # Xcode can "helpfully" switch back to Automatic signing during the build,
    # ignoring the profile match just fetched and using a different one → build fails.
    # Setting Manual + explicit profile name guarantees the correct cert is used.
    #
    # PROVISIONING_PROFILE_SPECIFIER naming convention for match:
    # "match AppStore com.example.app" — must match exactly.
    gym(
      scheme:           "demo_app",
      workspace:        "ios/demo_app.xcworkspace",
      configuration:    "Release",
      export_method:    "app-store",
      output_directory: "./build/ios",
      output_name:      "demo_app.ipa",
      include_bitcode:  false,  # WHY false: Apple deprecated bitcode since Xcode 14
      xcargs: [
        "CODE_SIGN_STYLE=Manual",
        "PROVISIONING_PROFILE_SPECIFIER='match AppStore #{ENV['APP_IDENTIFIER']}'",
        "CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY='iPhone Distribution'",
      ].join(" "),
    )

    # WHY pilot (= upload_to_testflight):
    # skip_waiting_for_build_processing: true → Apple takes 5-30 min to process the build.
    # CI doesn't need to wait — the build appears in TestFlight automatically once Apple finishes.
    # distribute_external: false → internal testers only (no Apple review required).
    pilot(
      api_key:                           api_key,
      ipa:                               "./build/ios/demo_app.ipa",
      skip_waiting_for_build_processing: true,
      distribute_external:               false,
      changelog:                         release_notes,
    )

    version = get_version_number(xcodeproj: "ios/demo_app.xcodeproj", target: "demo_app")
    UI.success "✅ iOS #{version} (#{new_build_number}) → TestFlight!"

    notify_slack(
      message: "🍎 iOS #{version} (#{new_build_number}) uploaded to TestFlight!",
      payload: { "Release Notes" => release_notes },
    )
  end

  # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  #  production
  #  Submit build to App Store for Apple review
  #
  #  WHY two-step workflow (beta → production):
  #  - Step 1 (beta): QA tests on TestFlight, confirms stable
  #  - Step 2 (production): Submit the QA-approved build to App Store
  #  No rebuild needed — Apple uses the binary already in TestFlight
  #
  #  IMPORTANT: Set up metadata + screenshots before running this lane
  #  for the first time. Set skip_metadata: false, skip_screenshots: false when ready.
  # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  desc "Submit build to App Store for review. Run after QA has approved the build on TestFlight."
  lane :production do
    api_key = asc_api_key
    version = get_version_number(xcodeproj: "ios/demo_app.xcodeproj", target: "demo_app")

    # WHY upload_to_app_store (alias: deliver):
    # submit_for_review: true → automatically submits after upload, no need to go to App Store Connect
    # automatic_release: false → Apple approves but does NOT auto-release
    #   Team manually clicks "Release this version" — avoids accidental releases
    # force: true → skip HTML report verification (no browser on CI)
    # skip_metadata/skip_screenshots: true → not set up yet, enable when ready
    upload_to_app_store(
      api_key:           api_key,
      app_identifier:    ENV["APP_IDENTIFIER"],
      submit_for_review: true,
      automatic_release: false,
      force:             true,
      skip_metadata:     true,
      skip_screenshots:  true,
      # WHY no .ipa passed: deliver picks the latest build from TestFlight.
      # No need to re-upload the binary — saves time.
    )

    notify_slack(
      message: "🚀 iOS #{version} submitted for App Store review! Apple typically takes 1-3 days.",
    )
    UI.success "✅ iOS #{version} submitted for review!"
  end

  # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  #  adhoc
  #  Build .ipa for ad-hoc distribution via direct link (Diawi, Firebase)
  #  No App Store needed, no TestFlight install required.
  #  Limitation: only installs on devices registered in Apple Developer Portal.
  # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  desc "Build .ipa for ad-hoc distribution via Diawi or Firebase Distribution"
  lane :adhoc do
    api_key = asc_api_key
    match(
      type:                    "adhoc",
      readonly:                true,
      api_key:                 api_key,
      app_identifier:          ENV["APP_IDENTIFIER"],
      git_url:                 ENV["MATCH_GIT_URL"],
      git_basic_authorization: Base64.strict_encode64("x-access-token:#{ENV['MATCH_GIT_TOKEN']}"),
    )
    gym(
      scheme:           "demo_app",
      workspace:        "ios/demo_app.xcworkspace",
      configuration:    "Release",
      export_method:    "ad-hoc",
      output_directory: "./build/ios",
      output_name:      "demo_app_adhoc.ipa",
      include_bitcode:  false,
      xcargs: [
        "CODE_SIGN_STYLE=Manual",
        "PROVISIONING_PROFILE_SPECIFIER='match AdHoc #{ENV['APP_IDENTIFIER']}'",
        "CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY='iPhone Distribution'",
      ].join(" "),
    )
    UI.success "✅ Adhoc build: ./build/ios/demo_app_adhoc.ipa"
  end

  # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  #  build_only
  #  Build .ipa only, no upload. Use to verify build config is not broken.
  # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  desc "Build .ipa only (no upload) — verify build config"
  lane :build_only do
    gym(
      scheme:           "demo_app",
      workspace:        "ios/demo_app.xcworkspace",
      configuration:    "Release",
      export_method:    "app-store",
      output_directory: "./build/ios",
      output_name:      "demo_app.ipa",
      include_bitcode:  false,
      xcargs:           "-allowProvisioningUpdates",
    )
    UI.success "✅ Build complete: ./build/ios/demo_app.ipa"
  end

  # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  #  bump_version
  #  Increment version number (major/minor/patch). Run before a release.
  #  Example: bundle exec fastlane ios bump_version type:minor
  # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  desc "Increment version number. Param: type (major|minor|patch). Example: bundle exec fastlane ios bump_version type:minor"
  lane :bump_version do |options|
    bump_type = options[:type] || "patch"
    increment_version_number(
      bump_type:  bump_type,
      xcodeproj:  "ios/demo_app.xcodeproj",
    )
    version = get_version_number(xcodeproj: "ios/demo_app.xcodeproj", target: "demo_app")
    UI.success "✅ iOS version bumped to #{version}"
  end

  # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  #  distribute_qa
  #  Build QA scheme → distribute to BOTH:
  #   ① TestFlight (app-store signed IPA) — unlimited testers
  #   ② Firebase App Distribution (ad-hoc signed IPA) — registered UDIDs
  #
  #  WHY 2 channels:
  #  - TestFlight: cho tester không cần đăng ký UDID, install qua App Store
  #  - Firebase: cho tester cần install nhanh, không chờ TestFlight processing
  #
  #  WHY build số phụ lấy từ ASC:
  #  TestFlight yêu cầu build number tăng đơn điệu — không thể dùng github.run_number
  #  vì mỗi lần CI chạy mới không biết số trước đó là bao nhiêu.
  # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  desc "Build QA → TestFlight (app-store) + Firebase App Distribution (ad-hoc)"
  lane :distribute_qa do
    api_key      = asc_api_key
    qa_app_id    = ENV.fetch("QA_APP_IDENTIFIER",   "com.tuanvu.demoapp.qa")
    version_name = ENV.fetch("APP_VERSION",          "1.0.0")

    # ── Step 1: Resolve build number ───────────────────────────
    latest_build = latest_testflight_build_number(
      api_key:              api_key,
      app_identifier:       qa_app_id,
      initial_build_number: 0,
    )
    new_build_number = latest_build + 1
    increment_build_number(
      build_number: new_build_number,
      xcodeproj:    "ios/demo_app.xcodeproj",
    )

    # ── Step 2: Badge QA icon ───────────────────────────────────
    # WHY add_badge: tester phân biệt QA build vs Prod ngay trên home screen.
    # CI runner là ephemeral — icon thay đổi chỉ tồn tại trong run đó, không commit.
    # shield_scale 0.75 → badge nhỏ gọn, không che nội dung icon.
    add_badge(
      shield:           "QA-#{version_name}-orange",
      shield_scale:     "0.75",
      shield_no_resize: true,
      glob:             "/ios/demo_app/Images.xcassets/AppIcon.appiconset/*.png",
    )

    # ── Step 3: TestFlight (app-store IPA) ─────────────────────
    match(
      type:                    "appstore",
      readonly:                true,
      api_key:                 api_key,
      app_identifier:          qa_app_id,
      git_url:                 ENV["MATCH_GIT_URL"],
      git_basic_authorization: Base64.strict_encode64("x-access-token:#{ENV['MATCH_GIT_TOKEN']}"),
    )

    gym(
      scheme:           "demo_app-QA",
      workspace:        "ios/demo_app.xcworkspace",
      configuration:    "Release-QA",
      export_method:    "app-store",
      output_directory: "./build/ios",
      output_name:      "demo_app_qa.ipa",
      include_bitcode:  false,
      xcargs: [
        "CODE_SIGN_STYLE=Manual",
        "PROVISIONING_PROFILE_SPECIFIER='match AppStore #{qa_app_id}'",
        "CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY='iPhone Distribution'",
        "ENVFILE=.env.qa",
      ].join(" "),
    )

    # WHY no changelog: pilot with skip_waiting_for_build_processing: true +
    # changelog causes it to wait for build to appear in ASC just to attach
    # the changelog — defeating the purpose of skipping. QA builds don't need
    # a changelog in TestFlight (release notes go to Firebase instead).
    pilot(
      api_key:                           api_key,
      ipa:                               "./build/ios/demo_app_qa.ipa",
      app_identifier:                    qa_app_id,
      skip_waiting_for_build_processing: true,
      distribute_external:               false,
    )
    UI.success "✅ QA #{version_name} (#{new_build_number}) → TestFlight!"

    # ── Step 4: Firebase (ad-hoc IPA) ──────────────────────────
    # WHY rebuild với adhoc thay vì reuse app-store IPA:
    # App-store signed IPA không install được trực tiếp — cần App Store.
    # Ad-hoc signed IPA install trực tiếp trên device đã đăng ký UDID.
    match(
      type:                    "adhoc",
      readonly:                true,
      api_key:                 api_key,
      app_identifier:          qa_app_id,
      git_url:                 ENV["MATCH_GIT_URL"],
      git_basic_authorization: Base64.strict_encode64("x-access-token:#{ENV['MATCH_GIT_TOKEN']}"),
    )

    gym(
      scheme:           "demo_app-QA",
      workspace:        "ios/demo_app.xcworkspace",
      configuration:    "Release-QA",
      export_method:    "ad-hoc",
      output_directory: "./build/ios",
      output_name:      "demo_app_qa_adhoc.ipa",
      include_bitcode:  false,
      xcargs: [
        "CODE_SIGN_STYLE=Manual",
        "PROVISIONING_PROFILE_SPECIFIER='match AdHoc #{qa_app_id}'",
        "CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY='iPhone Distribution'",
        "ENVFILE=.env.qa",
      ].join(" "),
    )

    firebase_app_distribution(
      app:                ENV.fetch("FIREBASE_IOS_QA_APP_ID", ""),
      groups:             "qa-testers",
      firebase_cli_token: ENV["FIREBASE_TOKEN"],
      ipa_path:           "./build/ios/demo_app_qa_adhoc.ipa",
      release_notes:      release_notes,
    )
    UI.success "✅ QA #{version_name} (#{new_build_number}) → Firebase App Distribution!"
  end

  # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  #  refresh_profile
  #  Run after adding a new device to Apple Developer Portal.
  #  WHY NOT revoking the cert: force_for_new_devices: true only regenerates
  #  the provisioning profile (including the new device), does not touch the cert.
  #  Revoking the cert would break builds for the entire team.
  # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  desc "Refresh provisioning profile after adding a new device. Does not revoke the cert."
  lane :refresh_profile do
    api_key = asc_api_key
    ["development", "adhoc"].each do |type|
      match(
        type:                  type,
        readonly:              false,
        force_for_new_devices: true,
        api_key:               api_key,
        app_identifier:        ENV["APP_IDENTIFIER"],
        git_url:               ENV["MATCH_GIT_URL"],
        git_basic_authorization: Base64.strict_encode64("x-access-token:#{ENV['MATCH_GIT_TOKEN']}"),
      )
    end
    UI.success "✅ Development + AdHoc profiles refreshed!"
  end

  # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  #  register_new_device
  #  Register a new device in Apple Developer Portal.
  #  Automatically refreshes the profile so the device can install adhoc/dev builds.
  # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  desc "Register a new device in Apple Portal then refresh the development profile"
  lane :register_new_device do
    api_key     = asc_api_key
    device_name = prompt(text: "Device name (e.g. Antonio iPhone 15): ")
    device_udid = prompt(text: "Device UDID: ")

    # WHY register_devices adds the UDID to Apple Developer Portal (team level).
    # Without this → the device cannot install adhoc/dev builds.
    register_devices(
      devices: { device_name => device_udid },
      api_key: api_key,
    )

    match(
      type:                  "development",
      readonly:              false,
      force_for_new_devices: true,
      api_key:               api_key,
      app_identifier:        ENV["APP_IDENTIFIER"],
      git_url:               ENV["MATCH_GIT_URL"],
      git_basic_authorization: Base64.strict_encode64("x-access-token:#{ENV['MATCH_GIT_TOKEN']}"),
    )
    UI.success "✅ Device '#{device_name}' (#{device_udid}) registered!"
  end

  # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  #  error — Cleanup when a lane fails
  # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  error do |lane, exception|
    UI.error "❌ iOS lane :#{lane} failed: #{exception.message}"
    notify_slack(
      message: "❌ iOS lane :#{lane} failed!\n#{exception.message}",
      success: false,
    )
  end

end

# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
#  Android Platform
# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
platform :android do

  # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  #  beta
  #  Build .aab (Android App Bundle) → upload to Play Internal Testing
  #
  #  WHY AAB instead of APK:
  #  Google Play requires AAB since Aug 2021 for new apps.
  #  AAB is 15-20% smaller than APK; Google Play generates optimized APKs per device.
  #
  #  WHY Internal Testing:
  #  - No Apple-style review → publishes within minutes
  #  - Only emails invited in Play Console can see the build
  #  - After QA approval → promote to production (no rebuild needed)
  #
  #  NOTE: First upload MUST be done manually via Google Play Console.
  #  supply (fastlane) only works from the second upload onwards.
  # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  desc "Build .aab and upload to Google Play Internal Testing"
  lane :beta do
    # WHY query versionCode from Play Store:
    # Same reason as iOS: CI runners are ephemeral, can't persist state.
    # versionCode in build.gradle is always stale → query real-time.
    # rescue: first time ever (internal track has no builds yet) → default to 0.
    # WHY ANDROID_APP_IDENTIFIER: iOS uses APP_IDENTIFIER (com.tuanvu.demoapp),
    # Android package name is different — must not share the same env var.
    package_name = ENV["ANDROID_APP_IDENTIFIER"] || ENV["APP_IDENTIFIER"]

    current_version_code = begin
      google_play_track_version_codes(
        package_name: package_name,
        track:        "internal",
        json_key:     ENV["GOOGLE_PLAY_JSON_KEY_PATH"],
      ).max
    rescue
      0
    end || 0

    version_code = current_version_code + 1
    version_name = ENV["APP_VERSION"] || "1.0.0"
    # YARA pattern: CI injects ANDROID_BUILD_FLAVOUR → Fastfile reads dynamically
    # Local: default to "Prod" nếu không set env var
    flavour = ENV["ANDROID_BUILD_FLAVOUR"] || "Prod"

    UI.message "📦 Building #{flavour} #{version_name} (#{version_code})..."

    # WHY gradle task "bundle" (not "assemble"):
    # - "assemble" → .apk (Play Store rejects these since 2021)
    # - "bundle"   → .aab (App Bundle — required for Play Store)
    #
    # WHY signing via android.injected.signing.* properties:
    # This is an Android Gradle Plugin mechanism — passes signing credentials
    # externally WITHOUT hardcoding them in build.gradle.
    # These are not regular -P project properties — AGP handles them specially.
    gradle(
      task:        "bundle",
      flavor:      flavour,
      build_type:  "Release",
      project_dir: "android/",
      properties: {
        # Signing credentials — injected by AGP, no need to read in build.gradle
        "android.injected.signing.store.file"     => ENV["ANDROID_KEYSTORE_PATH"],
        "android.injected.signing.store.password" => ENV["ANDROID_KEYSTORE_PASSWORD"],
        "android.injected.signing.key.alias"      => ENV["ANDROID_KEYSTORE_ALIAS"],
        "android.injected.signing.key.password"   => ENV["ANDROID_KEY_PASSWORD"],
        # Version management — read via project.findProperty() in build.gradle
        "versionCode"                             => version_code,
        "versionName"                             => version_name,
      },
    )

    # WHY supply uploads to Internal track:
    # Internal Testing requires no review — publishes within minutes.
    # skip_upload_apk: true — we upload aab, not apk.
    # skip_upload_images/screenshots: true — no store listing update needed.
    supply(
      package_name:            package_name,
      track:                   "internal",
      aab:                     lane_context[SharedValues::GRADLE_AAB_OUTPUT_PATH],
      json_key:                ENV["GOOGLE_PLAY_JSON_KEY_PATH"],
      skip_upload_apk:         true,
      skip_upload_images:      true,
      skip_upload_screenshots: true,
      release_status:          "completed",
    )

    UI.success "✅ #{flavour} #{version_name} (#{version_code}) → Play Internal Testing!"

    # notify_slack(
    #   message: "🤖 Android #{flavour} #{version_name} (#{version_code}) uploaded to Play Internal Testing!",
    #   payload: { "Release Notes" => release_notes },
    # )
  end

  # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  #  firebase_beta
  #  Build APK + AAB → upload to Firebase App Distribution
  #
  #  YARA pattern: lane này tương đương android/fastlane/Fastfile:beta trong
  #  sh-yara-connect-mobile — fully dynamic qua ENV['ANDROID_BUILD_FLAVOUR'].
  #
  #  Khác biệt so với lane :beta (Google Play):
  #  - Dùng firebase_app_distribution thay vì supply
  #  - Không cần Google Play Console / service account
  #  - versionCode dùng github.run_number (từ CI) — Firebase không yêu cầu incremental
  #  - Build cả APK (assemble) lẫn AAB (bundle) — Firebase nhận cả 2
  # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  desc "Build APK + AAB → upload to Firebase App Distribution (non-production environments)"
  lane :firebase_beta do
    # YARA pattern: đọc flavor từ env var — CI inject, local dùng default
    flavour      = ENV["ANDROID_BUILD_FLAVOUR"] || "Antonio"
    version_code = ENV["APP_VERSION_CODE"]      || Time.now.strftime("%Y%m%d%H")
    version_name = ENV["APP_VERSION"]           || "1.0.0"

    UI.message "🔥 Building #{flavour} #{version_name} (#{version_code}) for Firebase..."

    gradle(task: "clean", project_dir: "android/")

    gradle(
      task:        "assemble",
      flavor:      flavour,
      build_type:  "Release",
      project_dir: "android/",
      properties: {
        "android.injected.signing.store.file"     => ENV["ANDROID_KEYSTORE_PATH"],
        "android.injected.signing.store.password" => ENV["ANDROID_KEYSTORE_PASSWORD"],
        "android.injected.signing.key.alias"      => ENV["ANDROID_KEYSTORE_ALIAS"],
        "android.injected.signing.key.password"   => ENV["ANDROID_KEY_PASSWORD"],
        "versionCode"                             => version_code,
        "versionName"                             => version_name,
      },
    )

    gradle(
      task:        "bundle",
      flavor:      flavour,
      build_type:  "Release",
      project_dir: "android/",
      properties: {
        "android.injected.signing.store.file"     => ENV["ANDROID_KEYSTORE_PATH"],
        "android.injected.signing.store.password" => ENV["ANDROID_KEYSTORE_PASSWORD"],
        "android.injected.signing.key.alias"      => ENV["ANDROID_KEYSTORE_ALIAS"],
        "android.injected.signing.key.password"   => ENV["ANDROID_KEY_PASSWORD"],
        "versionCode"                             => version_code,
        "versionName"                             => version_name,
      },
    )

    firebase_app_distribution(
      app:                   ENV["FIREBASE_APP_ID"],
      groups:                ENV["FIREBASE_GROUPS"] || "antonio-testers",
      # WHY firebase_cli_token: CI runner không có browser → không thể `firebase login`.
      # `firebase login:ci` tạo 1 token offline dùng được trên CI.
      firebase_cli_token:    ENV["FIREBASE_TOKEN"],
      release_notes:         release_notes,
      # WHY APK thay vì AAB: AAB yêu cầu Firebase project link với Google Play để process splits.
      # APK install trực tiếp trên device → không cần Google Play integration.
      # App Distribution dùng APK là đủ cho internal testers.
      android_artifact_type: "APK",
    )

    UI.success "✅ #{flavour} #{version_name} (#{version_code}) → Firebase App Distribution!"

    notify_slack(
      message: "🔥 Android #{flavour} #{version_name} (#{version_code}) → Firebase App Distribution!",
      payload: { "Release Notes" => release_notes },
    )
  end

  # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  #  production
  #  Promote build from Internal Testing → Production (staged rollout)
  #
  #  WHY no rebuild:
  #  The binary QA tested on the internal track is promoted to production.
  #  Rebuilding = risk of binary change → QA would need to start over.
  #
  #  Staged Rollout Strategy:
  #  - rollout: 0.1 → release to 10% of users
  #  - Monitor crash rate for 24-48h on Firebase Crashlytics/Sentry
  #  - Gradually increase: 0.25 → 0.5 → 1.0
  #  - If issues arise: halt rollout, hotfix, re-release
  # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  desc "Promote build from Internal Testing to Production with staged rollout"
  lane :production do
    rollout      = ENV["ROLLOUT_PERCENTAGE"] || "0.1"
    version_name = ENV["APP_VERSION"] || "1.0.0"

    # WHY track_promote_to (not re-uploading the AAB):
    # Takes the latest build from the internal track and promotes it to production.
    # Does not upload a new binary — this is the exact binary QA tested.
    supply(
      package_name:            ENV["ANDROID_APP_IDENTIFIER"] || ENV["APP_IDENTIFIER"],
      json_key:                ENV["GOOGLE_PLAY_JSON_KEY_PATH"],
      track:                   "internal",
      track_promote_to:        "production",
      rollout:                 rollout,
      skip_upload_apk:         true,
      skip_upload_aab:         true,
      skip_upload_images:      true,
      skip_upload_screenshots: true,
    )

    rollout_pct = (rollout.to_f * 100).to_i
    UI.success "✅ Android #{version_name} → Production (#{rollout_pct}% rollout)!"

    notify_slack(
      message: "🚀 Android #{version_name} released to Production (#{rollout_pct}% rollout)!",
    )
  end

  # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  #  build_only
  #  Build AAB only, no upload. Use to verify signing config.
  # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  desc "Build .aab only (no upload) — verify build + signing config"
  lane :build_only do
    # WHY flavor required: flavorDimensions defined → task "bundleRelease" does not exist.
    # Gradle expects "bundleProdRelease" — must pass flavor explicitly.
    flavour = ENV["ANDROID_BUILD_FLAVOUR"] || "Prod"
    gradle(
      task:        "bundle",
      flavor:      flavour,
      build_type:  "Release",
      project_dir: "android/",
      properties: {
        "android.injected.signing.store.file"     => ENV["ANDROID_KEYSTORE_PATH"],
        "android.injected.signing.store.password" => ENV["ANDROID_KEYSTORE_PASSWORD"],
        "android.injected.signing.key.alias"      => ENV["ANDROID_KEYSTORE_ALIAS"],
        "android.injected.signing.key.password"   => ENV["ANDROID_KEY_PASSWORD"],
      },
    )
    UI.success "✅ AAB: #{lane_context[SharedValues::GRADLE_AAB_OUTPUT_PATH]}"
  end

  # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  #  bump_version
  #  Update versionName in android/app/build.gradle.
  #  Example: bundle exec fastlane android bump_version version:2.1.0
  # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  desc "Update versionName in build.gradle. Example: bundle exec fastlane android bump_version version:2.1.0"
  lane :bump_version do |options|
    version = options[:version]
    UI.user_error!("Missing param: version. Example: bundle exec fastlane android bump_version version:2.1.0") unless version

    # WHY regex replace instead of android_set_version_name:
    # Simpler, no plugin needed, works with any build.gradle format.
    build_gradle = "../android/app/build.gradle"
    content = File.read(build_gradle)
    new_content = content.gsub(/versionName\s+"[^"]+"/, "versionName \"#{version}\"")
    File.write(build_gradle, new_content)
    UI.success "✅ Android versionName → #{version}"
  end

  # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  #  error — Cleanup when a lane fails
  # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  error do |lane, exception|
    UI.error "❌ Android lane :#{lane} failed: #{exception.message}"
    notify_slack(
      message: "❌ Android lane :#{lane} failed!\n#{exception.message}",
      success: false,
    )
  end

end
